From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:09:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: xpon: omci: keep the serial number from unprivileged
 users

The GPON serial number is what the OLT authenticates the ONU with, and
on some networks it is the only credential. Any local user could read
it: the serial_number attribute in sysfs was 0644, and the MIB get and
MIB next commands of the Generic Netlink family, which return the ONU-G
and circuit pack objects that hold it, had no permission flag. The
password attribute is write only and the config get command already
asks for CAP_NET_ADMIN.

On an OpenWrt router the services that face the network and do not run
as root, dnsmasq, ntpd and hostapd, are the ones this matters for. Make
serial_number 0600 and require CAP_NET_ADMIN for MIB get and MIB next.
The status, class get and class next commands return no identity and
stay open.

Found in a security review of the OMCI agent.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/net/xpon/omci/core.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/core.c
@@ -1280,6 +1280,7 @@ static const struct genl_ops omci_genl_o
 	},
 	{
 		.cmd = OMCI_CMD_MIB_GET,
+		.flags = GENL_ADMIN_PERM,
 		.policy = omci_policy,
 		.doit = omci_cmd_mib_get,
 	},
@@ -1303,6 +1304,7 @@ static const struct genl_ops omci_genl_o
 	},
 	{
 		.cmd = OMCI_CMD_MIB_NEXT,
+		.flags = GENL_ADMIN_PERM,
 		.policy = omci_policy,
 		.doit = omci_cmd_mib_next,
 	},
--- a/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c
@@ -434,7 +434,8 @@ static ssize_t serial_number_store(struc
 	return omci_sysfs_string_store(omci_dev_from_dev(dev),
 				       OMCI_CONFIG_SERIAL_NUMBER, buf, count);
 }
-static DEVICE_ATTR_RW(serial_number);
+/* The serial number is what the OLT authenticates: not for every user. */
+static DEVICE_ATTR_ADMIN_RW(serial_number);
 
 static ssize_t password_store(struct device *dev,
 			      struct device_attribute *attr,
